    "setup_id": "05601a00c6bc4954635863826740b7b61d18798ad2f99e32a9fef415a652990f",
    "text": "To determine Melanie's average speed for the entire 1600 meter run, we need to calculate the total time she took to complete the run and then use the formula for average speed, which is total distance divided by total time.\n\nFirst, we calculate the time taken for each segment of the run.\n\n1. **First Segment:**\n   - Distance: 400 meters\n   - Speed: 5 m/s\n   - Time: \\(\\frac{400 \\text{ meters}}{5 \\text{ m/s}} = 80 \\text{ seconds}\\)\n\n2. **Second Segment:**\n   - Distance: 800 meters\n   - Speed: 4 m/s\n   - Time: \\(\\frac{800 \\text{ meters}}{4 \\text{ m/s}} = 200 \\text{ seconds}\\)\n\n3. **Third Segment:**\n   - Distance: 400 meters\n   - Speed: 8 m/s\n   - Time: \\(\\frac{400 \\text{ meters}}{8 \\text{ m/s}} = 50 \\text{ seconds}\\)\n\nNext, we sum the times for all three segments to find the total time taken for the 1600 meter run.\n\n\\[\n\\text{Total Time} = 80 \\text{ seconds} + 200 \\text{ seconds} + 50 \\text{ seconds} = 330 \\text{ seconds}\n\\]\n\nNow, we calculate the average speed using the total distance and total time.\n\n\\[\n\\text{Average Speed} = \\frac{\\text{Total Distance}}{\\text{Total Time}} = \\frac{1600 \\text{ meters}}{330 \\text{ seconds}}\n\\]\n\nTo express this as an improper fraction, we first simplify the fraction \\(\\frac{1600}{330}\\).\n\n1. **Simplify the fraction by finding the greatest common divisor (GCD) of 1600 and 330.**\n\n   - The prime factorization of 1600 is:\n     \\[\n     1600 = 2^6 \\times 5^2\n     \\]\n   - The prime factorization of 330 is:\n     \\[\n     330 = 2 \\times 3 \\times 5 \\times 11\n     \\]\n\n   - The common factors are \\(2\\) and \\(5\\). The GCD is:\n     \\[\n     \\text{GCD} = 2 \\times 5 = 10\n     \\]\n\n2. **Divide both the numerator and the denominator by their GCD:**\n\n   \\[\n   \\frac{1600 \\div 10}{330 \\div 10} = \\frac{160}{33}\n   \\]\n\nThus, Melanie's average speed for the 1600 meter run is:\n\n\\[\n\\boxed{\\frac{160}{33}}\n\\]",
